Replaced the 16-bit index table with a direct pointer table, eliminating the per-lookup index test and address arithmetic. Initialization remains one-time and preserves duplicate-number precedence, with the cold init branch hinted for the compiler.

```cpp
const Profile::MESG* Profile::GetMesg(const FIT_UINT16 num)
{
    static const MESG* lookup[65536] = {};
    static bool initialized = false;
    if (__builtin_expect(!initialized, 0))
    {
        for (int i = MESGS - 1; i >= 0; --i)
            lookup[mesgs[i].num] = &mesgs[i];
        initialized = true;
    }

    return lookup[num];
}
```